# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
RAG Management proxy for the universal multi-RAG platform (E5).

This router plugs the Radio Mar'ef frontend into the frozen E0 consumer flow:

    browser  ->  this proxy (same origin; holds the secrets)  ->  LiteLLM
    (Settings -> RAG Management / chat)                         (rag-* aliases)
                                                                 |
                                                                 v
    Central RAG Registry  <-  RAG Gateway (:8210)  <-  Providers

Rules (dedicated-rag: docs/contracts/CONSUMER_INTEGRATION_CONTRACT.md,
docs/architecture/MULTI_RAG_CONSUMER_ARCHITECTURE.md section 6):

  * consumers talk ONLY to the LiteLLM aliases ``rag-<rag_id>`` / ``rag-general``;
    they never call providers or the registry directly;
  * the Source Picker is fed by the registry's consumer-scoped
    ``GET /api/rag-registry/consumers/<id>/rags`` endpoint (E5-prep);
  * single selection  -> ``model = rag-<rag_id>``;
    multi selection   -> ``model = rag-general`` + ``sources = [selected ids]``;
  * the registry token and the consumer's LiteLLM virtual key are server-side
    secrets: read from the environment, NEVER echoed to the browser (section 8).

The module is INERT unless ``RAG_REGISTRY_URL`` + ``RAG_REGISTRY_TOKEN`` are
set; when inert, ``GET /api/rag/status`` reports ``configured: false`` and the
picker/chat endpoints answer 503 ``registry_unconfigured``. The legacy Neo4j
pipeline in api.py is untouched.

Upstream note: the gateway's own "streaming" is non-stream generation plus
sliced chunks (see drag/gateway/api.py), and LiteLLM relays OpenAI-shaped
chunks only — the gateway's final ``{citations, rag}`` meta event is not an
OpenAI chunk. The proxy therefore requests ``stream: false`` from LiteLLM and
re-emits the answer as SSE slices locally, preserving the radio frontend's
existing ``delta`` / ``sources`` / ``done`` / ``error`` SSE contract without
depending on unverified LiteLLM pass-through behaviour. Citations are always
taken from the gateway response — never fabricated.

E6.1 (Phase 3): a second, token-gated admin surface (``/api/rag/admin/*``)
lets an authorized operator — from the Radio's own admin panel — manage the
sources this consumer sees: provider list (with a live per-provider
``source_names`` book-title probe), enable/disable, priority/weight/top_k/
timeout edits with ``If-Match`` optimistic locking, connection/auth/
retrieval test probes, health, and master-prompt versioning. The admin
token is the ``RAG_ADMIN_TOKEN`` env var (separate from the registry
token, which never reaches the browser); the UI presents it in the
``x-rag-admin-token`` header. A wrong token yields 404 (no existence
leak); an unset token yields 503 ``admin_not_configured``. Every call is
forwarded to the central registry with the server-side registry token —
nothing is stored in the radio service.
"""
import hmac
import json
import os
import time
import uuid

import httpx
from concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor
from fastapi import APIRouter, Header, HTTPException
